a CA-signed host certificate, so clients trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) connect cleanly. Verified before and after a full node reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: openssh-server installed, ssh.socket active but no host keys existed yet\",\"Generated host keys via ssh-keygen -A\",\"Created dedicated CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca (ed25519, root-only private key)\",\"Signed the ed25519 host public key with the CA (ssh-keygen -s), producing /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with principals node1, 10.100.214.10, localhost, 52-week validity\",\"Added /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf with HostCertificate directive; validated config with sshd -t (after fixing missing /run/sshd)\",\"Restarted ssh service to load the certificate\",\"Verified with an SSH client trusting only the CA public key via @cert-authority in known_hosts and StrictHostKeyChecking=yes (no host key pinned) — connection accepted the cert, failing only later on publickey auth\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and service state on node1\",\"Scheduled and executed a native reboot (systemd-run + systemctl reboot) with the acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed changed boot_id proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified ssh.socket active, certificate files intact, and CA-trust-based client verification still succeeds post-reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH CA created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-58c4d034b4654ac6\"],\"summary\":\"Generated /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca ed25519 CA keypair with root-only permissions\"},{\"requirement\":\"Host certificate signed by the CA and installed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-84d7aefa132d4db6\",\"cmd-04755aaf44a6478a\",\"cmd-1d5b965733a4480e\",\"cmd-caf33fb09d74452b\"],\"summary\":\"Signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub, configured HostCertificate in sshd_config.d, validated config, restarted ssh, confirmed listening on :22\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client trusts CA (not pinned host key) and connects without pinning\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d650ad116b0f448f\",\"cmd-956547840e934566\"],\"summary\":\"known_hosts contained only an @cert-authority line (no pinned host key); ssh with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes reported 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate', failing only later on publickey auth\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fcf62c547d9b48a3\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id bfd05127-... and confirmed ssh.socket/ssh active plus cert files present before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0530b8445d1d4248\"],\"summary\":\"systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot and returned 'REBOOT_SCHEDULED' acknowledgement immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-adce91ad08fa4086\",\"cmd-b94516b1e8a5427b\",\"cmd-6116f73caee54ba1\"],\"summary\":\"Connection dropped mid-command during reboot, then reconnection showed new boot_id 56c34e23-... differing from baseline bfd05127-...\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services and cert data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3ad0676faba1419b\",\"cmd-56e93b108f60492d\"],\"summary\":\"ssh.socket active and listening on :22, CA and host-cert files intact, and CA-trust-only client verification again succeeded post-reboot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an SSH host certificate authority on node1 and configured sshd to present a CA-signed host certificate, so clients trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) connect cleanly. Verified before and after a full node reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: openssh-server installed, ssh.socket active but no host keys existed yet","Generated host keys via ssh-keygen -A","Created dedicated CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca (ed25519, root-only private key)","Signed the ed25519 host public key with the CA (ssh-keygen -s), producing /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with principals node1, 10.100.214.10, localhost, 52-week validity","Added /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf with HostCertificate directive; validated config with sshd -t (after fixing missing /run/sshd)","Restarted ssh service to load the certificate","Verified with an SSH client trusting only the CA public key via @cert-authority in known_hosts and StrictHostKeyChecking=yes (no host key pinned) — connection accepted the cert, failing only later on publickey auth","Captured baseline boot_id and service state on node1","Scheduled and executed a native reboot (systemd-run + systemctl reboot) with the acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed changed boot_id proving an actual restart","Re-verified ssh.socket active, certificate files intact, and CA-trust-based client verification still succeeds post-reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SSH CA created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-58c4d034b4654ac6"],"summary":"Generated /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca ed25519 CA keypair with root-only permissions"},{"requirement":"Host certificate signed by the CA and installed","command_ids":["cmd-84d7aefa132d4db6","cmd-04755aaf44a6478a","cmd-1d5b965733a4480e","cmd-caf33fb09d74452b"],"summary":"Signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub, configured HostCertificate in sshd_config.d, validated config, restarted ssh, confirmed listening on :22"},{"requirement":"Client trusts CA (not pinned host key) and connects without pinning","command_ids":["cmd-d650ad116b0f448f","cmd-956547840e934566"],"summary":"known_hosts contained only an @cert-authority line (no pinned host key); ssh with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes reported 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate', failing only later on publickey auth"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1","command_ids":["cmd-fcf62c547d9b48a3"],"summary":"Captured boot_id bfd05127-... and confirmed ssh.socket/ssh active plus cert files present before reboot"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-0530b8445d1d4248"],"summary":"systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot and returned 'REBOOT_SCHEDULED' acknowledgement immediately"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving actual restart","command_ids":["cmd-adce91ad08fa4086","cmd-b94516b1e8a5427b","cmd-6116f73caee54ba1"],"summary":"Connection dropped mid-command during reboot, then reconnection showed new boot_id 56c34e23-... differing from baseline bfd05127-..."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required services and cert data","command_ids":["cmd-3ad0676faba1419b","cmd-56e93b108f60492d"],"summary":"ssh.socket active and listening on :22, CA and host-cert files intact, and CA-trust-only client verification again succeeded post-reboot"}]},"ttft_ms":3091,"type":"result","duration_ms":109762,"uuid":"6cf55574-d637-4c36-aeab-52cd040f1ec9","ttft_stream_ms":2294,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":3090,"queued_turn_count":0}
